  "179:93": {
    "inputs": {
      "text": "Continuous five-second shot.\n\nThe small balloon-holding Todeok walks slowly along the center of the brown dirt path beside the stone fortress wall. From its starting position, it follows the curve of the path down toward the lower-left of the image, coming gently toward the camera. Its feet land only on the brown dirt surface, maintaining a clear gap from the stone wall on the right.\n\nTodeok takes a few short, evenly paced steps, covering only a small distance along the path. Its body faces slightly toward screen-left, aligned with the walking direction. Each foot lifts and lands naturally in alternation, with balanced strides and minimal sideways sway. The character remains small in the landscape.\n\nPreserve the original rounded body, face and short legs. Both wings retain their smooth, rounded, fingerless shapes. The holding wing keeps the same grip on the balloon strings, and the free wing stays close to the body. The four balloons follow with a gentle, small sway.\n\nSmooth lateral tracking shot: the camera slowly and steadily slides to the left, following Todeok along the path, so the curving stone fortress wall drifts gently to the right and the distant mountains shift slightly, keeping Todeok fully visible with its balloons. Keep the stone wall, mountains, path and soft evening light. The entire action stays on the dirt path: no stepping onto stones, climbing, jumping or approaching the lens.",
      "clip": [
        "179:84",
        0
      ]
    },
    "class_type": "CLIPTextEncode",
    "_meta": {
      "title": "CLIP Text Encode (Positive Prompt)",
      "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
      "ver": "0.3.45"
    }
  },
